     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left\\{ {\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{y = \\frac{2}{3}x + 1}\\\\\n{ - 2x + 3y = 5}\n\\end{array}} \\right.\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Test (–3, 3)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"3 = \\frac{2}{3}\\left( { - 3} \\right) + 1\"></span></td>\n<td>Substitute into the first equation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"3 =  - 2 + 1\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not true. This ordered pair is not a solution to the system. There is no need to test the second equation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
